  "_and_it_is_forgeable_by_the_commit_that_forges_the_file": "ROUND 69, THE COORDINATOR'S R68-C-02 (P3), declared here because a reader who sees 'the bytes of the program the test RUNNER executes' pinned may take the pin for unforgeable. It is not. One commit that patches node_modules/vitest/vitest.mjs, recomputes the one changed row here, and recomputes tools/law-bytes.json (which pins this file) passes: measured by the coordinator as S1 -- gate rc 0, 311 total, 0 skipped, 0 failed, with the attacker's module running inside the run. That is the SELF-CHECK LIMIT this phase has already accepted for the law's own byte pins, and it is bounded by REVIEW and not by this file: all three edits are visible in the diff a reviewer reads, and the lockfile row does not catch it because the installed bytes are not what `integrity` hashes. What the pin stops is an edit to the installed tree that does NOT come with its own re-pins.",
  "_how_the_tree_figures_were_counted": "ROUND 69, THE COORDINATOR'S R68-C-03 (P4), AND ROUND 70, ITS R69-C-01 (P4): the figures the whole-tree sentence weighed are carried HERE and nowhere above, because the clause that held them was deleted by the same commit that added this key and a reader following the word 'above' found nothing to check the command against. A whole-tree census was weighed and not taken at 24611 entries and 680571137 bytes, and the command is one line that runs from the repository root -- `/usr/bin/python3 -I -c \"import os; fs=[os.path.join(dp,f) for dp,dn,fn in os.walk('node_modules') for f in fn]; print(len(fs), sum(os.path.getsize(p) for p in fs if not os.path.islink(p) and os.path.isfile(p)))\"` -- which printed `24611 680571137` when the sentence was written and the same at round 69. The count depends on the RULE, which is why one is named: `find node_modules -type f | wc -l` gives 24572 (regular files only, symbolic links excluded) and `find node_modules -type f -o -type l | wc -l` gives 24619 (links counted as entries too). The figure above counts every directory entry that is not a directory, and sizes only the ones that are real files."
}
